          #ExamplesForTildeGInModLayer.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For the special case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is an ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ♭
                        %mi dR
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi flat
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G \simeq \Omega^{1}_{flat}(-,\mathfrak{g})
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiallyTiwstedGroup"}
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde G \simeq G
            %p
              On the other extreme, when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi p
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = \mathbf{B}^{p}U(1)
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle (p+1)-group
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiallyTiwstedGroup"}
              reduces to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              that characterizes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
              and hence yields
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi p
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi p
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi conn
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widetilde{\mathbf{B}^p U(1)}
                    \\simeq
                    \\mathbf{B}^p U(1)_{conn}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiallyTiwstedGroup"}
              is a certain non-abelian generalization of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TildeHatGIsDifferentialModuliBundle"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InterpretationOfTildeHatG"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              From example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesForTildeGInModLayer"}
              one see the conceptial meaning of def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiallyTiwstedGroup"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi flat
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G \simeq \Omega^1_{flat}(-,\mathfrak{g})
              (by the discussion
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "smooth+infinity-groupoid+--+structures#deRhamWithCoefficientsInBOfLieGroup"} here
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_G \colon G \to \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
              is a globally defined differential form. This is no longer the case for general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groups"} smooth ∞-groups
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+forms"} Maurer-Cartan forms
              here is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformations"} higher gauge transformations
              given by lower degree forms.
            %p
              But the WZW terms that we are after are supposed to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantizations"} prequantizations
              of globally defined Maurer-Cartan forms. The homotopy pullback in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiallyTiwstedGroup"}
              is precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal construction
