          %h4#refinement_of_hodge_filtrations Refinement of Hodge filtrations
          #RefinementOfHodgeFiltration.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                refinement of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hodge+filtration"} Hodge filtration
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}
              along the cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
              is a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
              object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi flat
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1_{flat}(-,G) \in \mathbf{H}
              and a completion to a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi flat
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi μ
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi 𝔾
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ♭
                                  %mi dR
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi 𝔾
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Omega^1_{flat}(-,G)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\mu}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\Omega^2_{cl}(-,\mathbb{G})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\flat_{dR} \mathbf{c}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}
                    }
            %p
              We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde G
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              of this refinement along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_G
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mover
                                    %mi G
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Ω
                              %mi flat
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi θ
                                  %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\tilde G &amp;\stackrel{\theta_{\tilde G}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{\Omega}^1_{flat}(-,G)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    G &amp;\stackrel{\theta_G}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi p
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G} = \mathbf{B}^p U(1)
              the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} circle (p+1)-group
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              an ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              may be taken to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cocycle
              corresponding to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
              and then
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde G \simeq G
            %p
              On the opposite extreme, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi p
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = \mathbf{B}^p U(1)
              itself with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
              the identity, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi pU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde G = \mathbf{B}^pU (1)_{conn}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
              under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
              and
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stackification"} infinity-stackification
            %p
              Hence a more general case is a fibered product of these two, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde G
              is such that a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \longrightarrow \tilde G
              is equivalently a pair consisting of a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to G
              and of differential
              = succeed "-form" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
              with “tensor multiplet” fields on them, such as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
              and the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
          %h4#wzw_terms_2 WZW terms
          #WZWTermByUniversality.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              In the situation of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RefinementOfHodgeFiltration"}
              there is an essentially unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundle"} prequantization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi L
                      %mi WZW
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{L}_{WZW}
                    \\colon
                    \\tilde G
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}_{conn}
            %p of the closed differential form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mover
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mover
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi flat
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi μ
                    %msubsup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi cl
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu(\theta_{\tilde G})
                    \\colon
                    \\tilde G
                    \\stackrel{\theta_{\tilde G}}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^1_{flat}(-,G)
                    \\stackrel{\mu}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{\Omega}^2_{cl}(-,\mathbb{G})
            %p
              whose underlying
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔾
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modulating+morphism"} modulated
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/looping+and+delooping"} looping
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \mathbf{c}
              of the original cocycle.
            %p
              This we call the
              %em WZW term
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}
              with respect to the chosen refinement of the Hodge structure.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              The morphism in question is the image under forming
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
              of the morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
              diagrams
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi flat
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi G
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi μ
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi 𝔾
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ♭
                                  %mi dR
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ♭
                              %mi dR
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi 𝔾
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mi G
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi θ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                        %mi B
                                      %mi 𝔾
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi G
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi Ω
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi 𝔾
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Omega^1_{flat}(-,G) &amp;\stackrel{\mu}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega^2_{cl}(-,\mathbb{G})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}G
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\flat_{dR}\mathbf{c}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\flat_{dR}\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{\theta_G}} &amp;&amp;  \uparrow^{\mathrlap{\theta_{\mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}}}}
                    \\\
                    G &amp;\stackrel{\Omega \mathbf{c}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the top square is from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RefinementOfHodgeFiltration"}
              and where the bottom square is the naturality square of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
              that defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+forms"} Maurer-Cartan forms
              (see
